abstract: >-
  Natural-language control of a TurtleBot 4 ground robot, running entirely on
  local hardware. Speech is transcribed with faster-whisper, a local Qwen2.5-7B
  model turns the sentence into a plan, YOLOv8s-World locates the named object
  in the camera image, a 2-D LiDAR gives its range, and Nav2 drives to a
  stand-off pose. The language model only proposes: every motion passes
  deterministic guards before it reaches the base. The repository includes the
  packet captures and measurements behind the hardware findings, notably a Fast
  DDS heartbeat storm that was misdiagnosed twice as a thermal problem and then
  as a camera fault.
